        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block personal-section">
        <div class="wrap personal-grid">
          <div class="personal-text">
            <p class="eyebrow-label">Why This Project</p>
            <h2>Personal to Me</h2>
            <p>Growing up, two of my brothers, Nate and Jake, both used wheelchairs. They lived with epidermolysis bullosa, a condition that leaves the skin extremely fragile and prone to blistering which made even short trips outside the house genuinely difficult to plan for and navigate.</p>
            <p>As their brother, I realized how often people with disabilities are left out of everyday experiences and how rarely that gap gets addressed. Guide is my attempt at equity-focused design: building for a group that products have historically overlooked. When I became a designer, Guide had been an idea I had been thinking about for many years. It's the most personal project in this portfolio, and there's genuine intent behind it: making independent travel a little less uncertain for people who don't have the luxury of assuming a route will simply work for them.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="personal-photos">
            <img data-tilt src={img('personal-01.webp')} alt="Julian as a child with his brothers, one recovering from a bandaged arm, in a family photo" />
            <img data-tilt src={img('personal-02.webp')} alt="An earlier childhood photo of Julian with his brothers Nate and Jake" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="head-block head-block-tail">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="pull-quote" data-typewriter>
            <span aria-hidden="true"><span class="tw-seg" data-full="How can I help users in wheelchairs "></span><span class="tw-seg pull-quote-highlight" data-full="feel confident while traveling, especially alone"></span><span class="tw-seg" data-full="?"></span></span>
